e_TIRED%2C_TAKE_A_NAP._%283629160713%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":400,"thumbheight":266,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/IF_YOU%27re_TIRED%2C_TAKE_A_NAP._%283629160713%29.jpg/960px-IF_YOU%27re_TIRED%2C_TAKE_A_NAP._%283629160713%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/IF_YOU%27re_TIRED%2C_TAKE_A_NAP._%283629160713%29.jpg/500px-IF_YOU%27re_TIRED%2C_TAKE_A_NAP._%283629160713%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":400,"height":266,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/IF_YOU%27re_TIRED%2C_TAKE_A_NAP._%283629160713%29.jpg/960px-IF_YOU%27re_TIRED%2C_TAKE_A_NAP._%283629160713%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/08/IF_YOU%27re_TIRED%2C_TAKE_A_NAP._%283629160713%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IF_YOU%27re_TIRED,_TAKE_A_NAP._(3629160713).jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=56597390","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"<p>Drawing Contemporaries, curated by Eyebeam senior fellow Michael Mandiberg, is an exhibition of work on paper made by a peer group of new media artists who all create drawings, both as a primary object and as an experimental process. The exhibition includes work from Darren Kraft, Steve Lambert &amp; Julia Schwadron, Michael Mandiberg, Marisa Olson, and Lee Walton. For many of the artists, the use of computers and algorithms are the focus in their work. While a number of the artists are Eyebeam affiliated, all are contemporaries whose influences upon each other can be traced in this exhibition. Drawing Contemporaries will remain on exhibit through June 9, 2009.\n</p><p>Darren Kraft uses powdered graphite to photorealistically reproduce icons and logos associated with consumer and political culture; Eyebeam senior fellow Steve Lambert and Julia Schwadron write personal and poetic messages of hope which they leave taped up in public places; Michael Mandiberg uses the laser cutter to etch and carve works on paper that incorporate text, history and design; Marisa Olson performs Google image searches for obsolete technologies, and traces their contours directly off her laptop screen with a mechanical pencil; and Lee Walton creates elaborate indexes of possible graphic marks which are algorithmically used to document events as they occur. His subjects range from from pedestrian traffic to sports games.\n</p>\nDrawing Contemporaries was on view through June 9, 2009","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2009-05-26 14:57","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/people/42586873@N00\">Michael Mandiberg</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 2.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}}}]},"127725216":{"pageid":127725216,"ns":6,"title":"File:Rita Ora Celebrates 100 Years of the Coca-Cola at Contour Centenary Bar in 2015.jpg","index":3,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":1020662,"width":1200,"height":1801,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Rita_Ora_Celebrates_100_Years_of_the_Coca-Cola_at_Contour_Centenary_Bar_in_2015.jpg/500px-Rita_Ora_Celebrates_100_Years_of_the_Coca-Cola_at_Contour_Centenary_Bar_in_2015.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":400,"thumbheight":600,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Rita_Ora_Celebrates_100_Years_of_the_Coca-Cola_at_Contour_Centenary_Bar_in_2015.jpg/960px-Rita_Ora_Celebrates_100_Years_of_the_Coca-Cola_at_Contour_Centenary_Bar_in_2015.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Rita_Ora_Celebrates_100_Years_of_the_Coca-Cola_at_Contour_Centenary_Bar_in_2015.jpg/500px-Rita_Ora_Celebrates_100_Years_of_the_Coca-Cola_at_Contour_Centenary_Bar_in_2015.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":400,"height":600,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Rita_Ora_Celebrates_100_Years_of_the_Coca-Cola_at_Contour_Centenary_Bar_in_2015.jpg/960px-Rita_Ora_Celebrates_100_Years_of_the_Coca-Cola_at_Contour_Centenary_Bar_in_2015.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/47/Rita_Ora_Celebrates_100_Years_of_the_Coca-Cola_at_Contour_Centenary_Bar_in_2015.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rita_Ora_Celebrates_100_Years_of_the_Coca-Cola_at_Contour_Centenary_Bar_in_2015.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=127725216","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Rita Ora kicked off celebrations to mark the 100th anniversary of the iconic Coca-Cola Bottle at the opening of the Contour Centenary Bar in London, UK on March 19, 2015.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2015-03-19 09:07:00","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/phototoday2008/\">See Li</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY 2.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}}}]}}}}